1
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:04,879
Who gives a damn?

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,779
Who sleeps with whom?

3
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:26,275
Air Force One was headed for Beijing in May
when Marco Rubio told Donald Trump that U.S.

4
00:00:26,275 --> 00:00:31,311
intelligence had linked NVIDIA’s CEO to a
suspected Chinese spy.

5
00:00:31,311 --> 00:00:36,347
That’s what The New York Times and The
Washington Post reported.

6
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:45,880
The plane stopped for fuel in Anchorage.
Jensen Huang got on.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,202
Six months later, a reporter asked Trump if
he knew about it at the time.

8
00:01:00,202 --> 00:01:03,266
“No, I didn’t hear about it then,” he said.

9
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:08,347
According to the Times,

10
00:01:08,347 --> 00:01:12,476
Rubio’s warning was at least the second time
Trump had been briefed.

11
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:18,705
Apparently the president’s memory had a
longer layover than the plane.

12
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:37,642
The Times also reported a separate relationship between Huang and
an NVIDIA executive who reported directly to him.

13
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,944
Alice Huang had been an executive at
Singapore-based chip buyer Megaspeed.

14
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,976
The Times and the Post reported that U.S.

15
00:01:52,976 --> 00:01:56,315
intelligence concluded she worked for
Beijing—

16
00:01:56,315 --> 00:01:59,799
an allegation China’s foreign ministry
rejected.

17
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:09,953
The Information, citing people who know her,
an NVIDIA China sales employee,

18
00:02:09,953 --> 00:02:11,604
and corporate records,

19
00:02:11,604 --> 00:02:22,408
reported that her relationship with Jensen Huang helped get at least $7.5 billion
worth of NVIDIA chips through intermediaries to Chinese firms.

20
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:28,749
NVIDIA’s board said on November 8, when it
opened its inquiry,

21
00:02:28,749 --> 00:02:35,614
that it had no reason to believe national
security or NVIDIA secrets were compromised.

22
00:02:35,614 --> 00:02:36,014
Fine.

23
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:38,926
Who signed off on the shipments?

24
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:45,448
Where did the chips go? What did NVIDIA tell
investors about the customer?

25
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,927
On Wednesday, November 11,

26
00:02:49,927 --> 00:02:57,536
The Wall Street Journal and Reuters reported that
NVIDIA’s board was preparing to oust Huang.

27
00:02:57,536 --> 00:03:03,590
As of early November 12, the company had yet
to announce a final decision.

28
00:03:08,450 --> 00:03:13,512
The stock fell more than 8 percent in
Wednesday’s after-hours trading.

29
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:28,166
Now consider a hypothetical scenario: a 30 percent crash across the
wider market would take a much bigger chain reaction—

30
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:28,484
say,

31
00:03:28,484 --> 00:03:35,478
a hypothetical pullback where a cloud company pushes
its next chip order into next year,

32
00:03:35,478 --> 00:03:41,120
and a lender demands actual revenue before
funding another data center.

33
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:47,605
That’s how a boardroom scandal could start
to look like the dot-com bust.

34
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:57,312
Meanwhile, Wall Street spent Wednesday
evening, November 11, dumping NVIDIA.

35
00:03:57,312 --> 00:04:04,996
On Thursday, November 19, if the IPO goes ahead as
scheduled, it gets to buy Anthropic.

36
00:04:07,050 --> 00:04:12,476
Read the November 10 prospectus before you
call that a change of heart.

37
00:04:12,476 --> 00:04:14,769
At the assumed midpoint price,

38
00:04:14,769 --> 00:04:25,162
NVIDIA itself has agreed to buy about $10 billion of non-voting Anthropic
stock in a concurrent private placement contingent on the IPO.

39
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:36,726
The board can show Jensen Huang the door.

40
00:04:39,050 --> 00:04:41,140
Somebody still has to sign the check.
